 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Depends on the reconstruction method. Point-wise reconstruction has complexity $O(m^3 n^3)$, while block-wise reconstruction reduces this to $O(3mn^3)$, offering an efficiency factor of $k = m^2/3$ [S3, unofficial]. Wavelet splatting Method 1 has complexity decaying with $2^j$ per scale, while Method 2 decays with $2^{3j}$ [S4].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Lossless compression decoding is serial and may require decompressing the whole volume in main memory unless optimized [S1, unofficial]. Adaptive methods reduce memory usage by only decompressing necessary blocks [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Measured Performance:** On MR-MRI data, 3-D CB-EZW achieved lossless rates of 2.285 and 2.195 bit/voxel [S5].
-*   **Strengths:** High compression ratios, support for multi-resolution rendering, and efficient storage of large datasets [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Serial nature of lossless decoding makes GPU implementation difficult [S1, unofficial]. Redundant computation in block-wise reconstruction [S3, unofficial].
-*   **When to use:** Large-scale time-varying data visualization on PC clusters or workstations [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When not to use:** When real-time interactive rendering on GPU is required with lossless compression and no specific optimizations are used [S1, unofficial].
