 ## Background
-Wavelet-based volume rendering originated from the application of wavelet transforms to volumetric data compression and rendering. It has been thoroughly studied by researchers in recent years, with overviews provided by Stollnitz et al. [S1, unofficial]. The method is used in frameworks like WTSP (Wavelet-based Time-Space Partitioning) tree for large-scale time-varying data visualization on PC clusters [S1, unofficial]. The technique leverages the multi-resolution properties of wavelets to enable adaptive rendering and efficient data storage [S1, unofficial].
